 80  of the excised breast mass  There are some nodular areas up to 0 5cm  which are nearest to the superior margin  0 5cm    In the adjacent adipose tissue  multiple fat necrosis measuring up to 0 6cm in diameter  which abuts the inferior anterior surface of the excised breast mass  SECTION CODE  B  Most lateral slice  posterior part with fibrous mass abutting the superior and inferior margin C  Third slice from lateral posterior part D  Third slice from lateral  middle part of the mass  abutting inferior margin E  Fourth slice from lateral  middle part of the specimen  fibrous mass  with some nodularity  maximum distance to the superior margin  0 7cm F  Fifth most lateral slice of the excised mass  middle part  with focal hemorrhages of about 0 1cm  fat necrosis  diameter 0 4cm  1 0cm away from the superior margin G  Sixth most lateral slice from the lateral margin  focally patchy  fibrous area  posterior part of the excised mass H  Sixth most lateral slice of the excised mass  anterior part containing skin ellipse I  Seventh most lateral slice  fibrous area with adjacent adipose tissue  posterior aspect of the excised breast mass J  Eighth most lateral slice of the breast mass  anterior  superior surface containing fat necrosis  slice that contained the superior stitch K  Ninth most lateral slice of the excised breast mass  posterior part L  Macroscopically uninvolved breast tissue  in the second most lateral slice of the excised mass  containing skin ellipse M  Macroscopically uninvolved breast tissue from the most medial slice Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  PART B  BR