The dense fibrous area is 1cm from the closest posterior margin  In the 10 o clock position in the medial aspect of the breast there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm diffuse blue discoloration to the breast tissue  Within this area there is a 0 6cm area of hemorrhage which is 1 5cm from the closest posterior margin and 1 1cm from the closest anterior margin  Cassette A contains the area of hemorrhage entirely submitted  Cassette B contains the closest posterior margin to the hemorrhagic area  Cassette C contains the closest anterior margin to the hemorrhagic area  Cassette D contains additional anterior margin  Cassette E contains additional blue dyed parenchyma and posterior margin  Within the areas of dense breast tissue there is a small 0 3cm focus of hemorrhage which is 2 5cm from the closest posterior margin  The entire area is submitted in cassette F  Additional sections of fibrocystic areas submitted in G  Possible axillary lymph nodes are submitted in cassette H  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm section of fatty tissue containing two lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The largest node is bisected and is submitted along with the smaller area entirely frozen as fx 1  and submitted in cassette I  The remainder of the tissue entirely submitted as cassette J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast bisopy scar  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan pink triangular piece of skin excised to a depth of 0 5cm  No clearly identifiable scar is noted on the surface  Two representative sections of skin are submitted in submitted in K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  skin right breast status post mastectomy  is a 14 x 3 5cm tan pink skin ellipse with little to no 