Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  positive margins  positive SNB  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  UNORIENTED FINAL MARGIN   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  HEALING SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY SITE  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  re excision left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  received with a long suture designating the lateral aspect and short suture designating the superior aspect  as per the surgeon  The short suture is located within the smooth  glistening previous biopsy cavity  which surfaces the entire superior aspect of the specimen  The superior aspect is therefore left uninked and the remainder of the specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  inferior   yellow  Sectioning reveals that the cavity fully abuts all of the margins  with the exception of the inferior margin  which is 0 6cm from the cavity  The remaining cut surfaces consist of yellow  lobulated adipose tissue  with no discrete masses grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative body of specimen  from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end  serially sectioned  Received fresh  labeled  final margin left breast   are 2 unoriented fragments of friable fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  each of which are serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   are multiple portions of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  which are dissected and palpated to reveal multiple candidate lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 2cm in greatest dimension  The largest candidate node is bisected to reveal a 0 6cm in greatest dimension cavity  with peripheral yellow discoloration  consistent with fat necrosis  This area may be consistent with the site of the previous sentinel node biopsy  All candidate nods are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate intact node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing 3 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing 1 candidate node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest candidate node  serially sectioned  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 15   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 40 14AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left  Re  Excision PART B  Breast  Left  Final Margin   Excision PART C  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla Contents   Dissection  report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
