e and chalky yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The biopsy cavity is involving the superior margin  0 2cm from the medial margin  0 7cm from the lateral margin  0 5cm from the inferior margin  and 0 1cm from the anterior margin and 0 1cm from the posterior margin  The dense white fibrous tissue abut the medial margin  inferior margin  and superior margin  and 1 5cm from the lateral margin  0 4cm from the anterior margin  and abuts the posterior margin  There are two white metal clips identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior end en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central portion submitted in sequential order   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain clip    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior end  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  additional superior margin B   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm yellow unoriented yellow tan fibrous adipose tissue  with one surface displaying a chalky white and shaggy appearance consistent with a biopsy cavity  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal white dense fibrous tissue  yellow chalky lobulated adipose tissue and one white metal clip  The specimen is submitted in its entirety labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains clip   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  RE  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
