Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 42 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  APOCRINE TYPE  SLIDE C   IN THE REGION OF THE BIOPSY SITE  RADIAL SCAR  EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The examined resection margins appear free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Several of the lymph nodes contain pigment laden macrophages  para cortical hyperplasia and subcapsular monocytoid B cell proliferations consistent with dermatopathic lymphadenopathy  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 20 21                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate parts  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm section of breast  partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 7 7cm ellipse of white pink skin  Eccentrically located on the skin ellipse is a 5 0cm in maximal diameter ill defined areola centered by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nipple  Opposite to the areola a 3 7cm long well healed linear scar  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm scarred biopsy cavity located with 0 7cm of the closest resection margin  Biopsy cavity is centered by white gray tissue  focally hemorrhagic and extends with multiple white gray fibrous bands to reach the inked resection margin  an additional area of yellow slightly firmed breast parenchyma is closer to the biopsy cavity  Section Code  A E  biopsy cavity  representative section in relation to closest resection margin F  slightly dense breast parenchyma  representative section GandH  additional representative sections Labeled  stitch a highest axillary node  left breast axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm soft tissue mass consisting mostly of adipose tissue  One of the fragment of adipose tissue is designated with a stitch  and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  I  lymph node  designated by surgeon with a stitch J P  lymph nodes  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  27 AUG 98 at 11 18 CLINICAL DATA  Previous excision for invasive ductal carcinoma with close margins reviewed at Brigham and Women s Hospital  Previous lymph dissection with positive in one of fifteen nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  FIBROADENOMA  SKIN  SITE UNDESIGNATED   NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 26                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a simple mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  an overlying 5 x 3cm skin ellipse with a 3cm curved healing incision  Beneath this  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm stellate  hard  white pink mass grossly consistent with healing biopsy site  extending to 0 4cm from the deep margin  Adjacent to the ill defined mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  rubbery nodule  Approximately 0 4cm anteriorly of this mass  is a 0 5cm biopsy cavity  The remaining parenchyma is mostly adipose tissue with focally  white and fibrotic areas and well defined firm nodules as large as 0 8cm  SECTION CODE A  Mass with deep margin and the biopsy cavity wall  B  Mass with deep margin and one firm nodule  C  Another representative section of mass with deep margin  D  Additional representative sections of the mass  E  Representative sections of the firm nodules  F  Representative sections of the uninvolved parenchyma  Also received in the same container is an unremarkable fragment of skin measuring 8cm in diameter  0 2cm 