Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 AUG 98 at 13 20 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision of left breast ductal carcinoma  invasive  Old biopsy cavity went to pectoralis  Also  mass in axilla                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING A SHORT DISTANCE FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY  AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Note  No residual invasive ductal carcinoma is seen  No angiolymphatic invasion is identified  BREAST  LEFT AXILLARY MASS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN AT MULTIPLE FOCI  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ONE LYMPH NODE  FREE OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA  Note  The axillary mass probably represents an invasive carcinoma arising in axillary breast tissue  The invasive lobular carcinoma surrounds  but does not invade  a single lymph node within the mass  No definitive angiolymphatic invasion is seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   MAPPING  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  Note  Keratin immunostains will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  07 AUG 98 at 19 04 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  Left Axilla   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained