Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 40 CLINICAL DATA  Inflammatory changes on physical exam with skin thickening and upper outer quadrant mass on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  PLEOMORPHIC TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definitive lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The tumor consists of pleomorphic cells growing in cords and clusters with a high mitotic rate and occasional intracytoplasmic lumina  Focally  the tumor resembles a high grade infiltrating ductal type carcinoma  although the predominant features are those of a pleomorphic infiltrating lobular carcinoma  Immunohistochemical stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported separately  Dr  Frederick Koerner has reviewed selected slides and agrees with the interpretation  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 39                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 29     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     Tumor does not extend to the overlying skin  dermis or epidermis   Added by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm overlying ellipse of skin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular firm white lesion  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in maximum dimension  2 0cm deep to the skin ellipse  A representative section of the lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted in A through K  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Incisional_biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 17 53 CLINICAL DATA  History of DCIS                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 14 35                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast reexcision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm yellow and tan fibrofatty soft tissue fragments  There is a short stitch     the anterior surface there is a long stitch marking the lateral surface  There is a bowtie stitch marking the cephalad surface  On the anterior surface there are several sutures which are closing off a previous biopsy cavity  There are no other gross abnormalities on the external surface  The specimen is inked according to protocol  Cephalad green  caudad yellow  posterior black  anterior blue  The specimen is serially sectioned  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity centrally located within the tissue  Around the biopsy cavity there is dense tan fibrosis with a variegated color pattern ranging from tan to orange to red white  There is no uninvolved breast tissue present  Representative sections are submitted in cassette A J  Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  RE EXCISION , No_breast_biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Private Outside MGH MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Gabrielle Baker  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 78 year old woman with a history of IDC in the right breast diagnosis in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   S P radiation  tamoxifen  now with palpable mass in left breast and abnormal mammogram  BI RADD 5   now undergoing core biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy reveal infiltrating nests and cords of malignant epithelial cells with associated desmoplasia  The tumor cells are mostly small with increased nucleus to cytoplasm ratio and eccentrically placed nuclei  In some areas there is a prominent single file pattern suggesting a component of lobular differentiation  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin demonstrates focal weak staining in a minority of tumor cells  In the context of the morphologic findings  the immunohistochemical staining pattern suggests a component of lobular carcinoma or a poorly differentiated ductal carcinoma loss of expression of e cadherin  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left   are 4 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  122  to chromosome 17 signals  123  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Left   Core biopsy  report_end  , Core_biopsy.
