in all areas from lobular carcinoma in situ  which also appears to be present  Further compromising the evaluation is the extensive involvement of lobules and areas of sclerosing adenosis by in situ carcinoma of both types  Carcinoma in situ is present in at least 9 of 16 sections  BREAST  SUPERIOR   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  SINGLE SMALL FOCUS OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  UNCERTAIN IF DUCTAL OR LOBULAR TYPE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND CAUTERY CHANGES  BREAST  INFERIOR   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 01 at 16 53                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five specimens  Labeled  sentinel node  hot and blue level 1  left breast  count   REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_CASE_ID   and 232  are two fragments of yellow fibrofatty soft tissue each measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The smaller fragment is a blue tan node bisected and submitted entirely as A  The larger fragment contains multiple lymph nodes and submitted entirely as B C  Labeled  sentinel node  2  hot and blue upper level 1  count    REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment containing two small nodes each measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm submitted entirely as D  Labeled  re excision left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm yellow lobulated fibrofatty portion of breast oriented by a short suture designating the superior and long suture designating the lateral margins  The inferior portion of the specimen is remarkable for a hemorrhagic tan  red cavity  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The anterior aspect of the sp