D_DATE x 3 0cm tan pink unremarkable overlying skin contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm unremarkable nipple and areola  There is a 3 5cm well healed linear scar located 4 7cm from the nipple  On the posterior  deep  aspect there is a minimum amount of dark red attached muscle  A REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of retraction with adherent overlying muscle is identified on the posterior aspect and is located directly subjacent to the overlying scar  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior aspect is inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a diffusely dense rubbery white fibrotic cut surface with multiple cystic structures ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in maximum dimension and containing a cloudy green to gray serous fluid  Within this fibrous area there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm stellate  indurated tan white firm area which abuts the posterior deep margin and is contiguous with the posterior area of retraction  This area comes to within 1 1cm of the overlying scar and could be consistent with a previous biopsy site  Surrounding this area there is an moderate amount of focal tan yellow fat necrosis  No residual tumor is identified  Within the uninvolved remaining predominately dense fibrotic parenchyma no discrete masses or lesions are identified  No lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  K Q  Entire possible previous biopsy site R S  Fibrous area adjacent to possible biopsy site T V  Uninvolved densely fibrotic and cystic remaining parenchyma Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink unremarkable skin ellipse  The margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted in cassette W  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART A  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , No_breast_biopsy.
